A \emph{Lucas sequence with parameter $A\in{\mathbb Z}$} is a sequence $(x_n)_{n\in {\mathbb Z}}$ that satisfies the recursive relation 
\begin{equation}\label{eq:lucas-general-recurrence}
    x_{n+1}=Ax_n-x_{n-1}.
\end{equation}
Each such sequence is defined uniquely by two initial values, and we define two particular Lucas sequences with initial values $\psi_0(A)=0, \psi_1(A)=1$ as well as $\chi_0(A)=2, \chi_1(A)=A$.

\begin{equation}\label{eq:lucas-general-recurrence}
